"status\": \"mismatch\"\n  },\n  \"status\": \"validation_parameter_mismatch\",\n  \"submitted\": false,\n  \"tool_id\": \"toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/iuc/datamash_ops/datamash_ops/1.9+galaxy0\",\n  \"validation_status\": \"parameter_mismatch\"\n}\n\n\nFILE validation_response.json\nstate_inputs operations [{'__index__': 0, 'op_column': '1', 'op_name': 'count'}]\nkeys ['action', 'citations', 'creator', 'credentials', 'description', 'display', 'edam_operations', 'edam_topics', 'enctype', 'errors', 'form_style', 'has_parameters', 'help', 'help_format', 'hidden', 'hidden_versions', 'history_id', 'icon', 'id', 'inputs']\n{\n  \"action\": \"/tool_runner/index\",\n  \"citations\": true,\n  \"creator\": null,\n  \"credentials\": [],\n  \"description\": \"(operations on tabular data)\",\n  \"display\": true,\n  \"edam_operations\": [],\n  \"edam_topics\": [],\n  \"enctype\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n  \"errors\": {},\n  \"form_style\": \"regular\",\n  \"has_parameters\": true,\n  \"help\": \"<p class=\\\"infomark\\\"><strong>TIP:</strong> Input data must be TAB delimited. If the desired dataset does not appear in the input list, use <em>Text Manipulation-&gt;Convert</em> to convert it to <strong>Tabular</strong> type.</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Syntax</strong></p>\\n<p>This tools performs common operations (such as summing, counting, mean, standard-deviation) on input file, based on tabular data. The tool can also optionaly group the input based on a given field.</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><p class=\\\"first\\\">Find the average score in statistics course of college students, grouped by their college major. The input file has three fields (Name,Major,Score) and a header line:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\nName        Major            Score\\nBryan       Arts             68\\nGabriel     Health-Medicine  100\\nIsaiah      Arts             80\\nTysza       Business         92\\nZackery     Engineering      54\\n...\\n...\\n</pre>\\n</li>\\n<li><p class=\\\"first\\\">Grouping the input by the second column (<em>Major</em>), sorting the input, and performing operations <strong>mean</strong> and <strong>sample standard deviation</strong> on the third column (<em>Score</em>), gives:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\nGroupBy(Major)     mean(Score)   sstdev(Score)\\nArts               68.9474       10.4215\\nBusiness           87.3636       5.18214\\nEngineering        66.5385       19.8814\\nHealth-Medicine    90.6154       9.22441\\nLife-Sciences      55.3333       20.606\\nSocial-Sciences    60.2667       17.2273\\n</pre>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>Note that input needs sorting here, since the column used for grouping (<em>Major</em>) is not sorted.</p>\\n<p>This sample file is available at <a class=\\\"reference external\\\" href=\\\"http://www.gnu.org/software/datamash\\\">http://www.gnu.org/software/datamash</a> .</p>\\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong></p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><p class=\\\"first\\\">Using the UCSC RefSeq Human Gene Track, available at: <a class=\\\"reference external\\\" href=\\\"http://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/goldenPath/hg38/database/refGene.txt.gz\\\">http://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/goldenPath/hg38/database/refGene.txt.gz</a></p>\\n</li>\\n<li><p class=\\\"first\\\">List the number and identifiers of isoforms per gene. The gene identifier is in column 13, the isoform/transcript identifier is in column 2. Grouping by column 13 and performing <strong>count</strong> and <strong>Combine all values</strong> on column 2, gives:</p>\\n<pre class=\\\"literal-block\\\">\\nGroupBy(field-13)     count(field-2)     collapse(field-2)\\nA1BG                  1                  NM_130786\\nA1BG-AS1              \n\nFILE validation_parameter_provenance.json\n{\n  \"checked_parameter_count\": 11,\n  \"mismatches\": [\n    {\n      \"expected\": 6,\n      \"path\": \"operations|0|op_column\",\n      \"resolved\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"expected\": \"mean\",\n      \"path\": \"operations|0|op_name\",\n      \"resolved\": \"count\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"missing_paths\": [\n    \"operations|1|op_column\",\n    \"operations|1|op_name\"\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"mismatch\"\n}\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
